        <dd class="govuk-summary-list__value">A person is guilty of common assault if they intentionally or recklessly apply unlawful force to another, or cause that person to apprehend immediate unlawful force, without their consent. <a href="#" onclick="alert('Opens: L&P guidance')">(Criminal Justice Act 1988 s.39)</a></dd>
